<section class="section theme-white">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">What goes in, what comes out</h2>
    <div class="bp-io">
      <div>
        <h3>You provide</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Documents</strong>: script (.fdx, .pdf, .txt or .md), treatment, synopsis, brief, notes. One is enough; more is better.</li>
          <li><strong>The production</strong>: format, genre, length, episodes, budget level and a target total if you have one.</li>
          <li><strong>Time</strong>: where you start (development, pre-production, shoot or post), start date, deadline, shooting days if already known.</li>
          <li><strong>Notes</strong>: locations you already have, crew you bring, things to leave out.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>You get back</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>A complete budget</strong>: activities per phase with cost lines (crew, cast, equipment, locations, travel, catering, post, delivery), fees and contingency as percentages.</li>
          <li><strong>A plan</strong>: scenes with their breakdown, shooting days clustered by location, a crew list per activity and a day plan per shooting day.</li>
          <li><strong>A review</strong>: a second pass that looks for double counts, missing items, odd ratios and the distance to your target.</li>
          <li><strong>Three files</strong>: the budget file for the Budget Planner app, a Tubes export that imports straight into Tubes, and a summary (optionally as PDF).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section theme-light">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="bp-steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Create an account and connect the app</h3>
        <p>Sign up with your company name and email address. The portal gives you a connection code; paste it in the Budget Planner app on your Mac or Windows computer.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Submit a production</h3>
        <p>In the portal, start a new production: upload your documents, fill in what you know, add notes. The app picks it up and runs the planner, step by step, on your own computer. Prefer not to run it yourself? We can run it for you.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Receive the budget</h3>
        <p>When the planner is done, the production shows as delivered in the portal with the totals, the number of activities, shooting days and lines, and the verdict of the review. Download the files, leave a remark for the next run.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/resources/budget-planner/portal/#signup">Create an account</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/resources/budget-planner/portal/#login">Log in</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section theme-white" id="download">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-heading">The app</h2>
    <p class="lead">The Budget Planner is a desktop app for macOS and Windows. It also works as a standalone budgeting tool: cost structures (Tubes Commercial Format, Filmfonds, Movie Magic, Netflix-style top sheet), formulas on shooting days and episodes, versions, forecast and Excel export, all stored as files on your own computer.</p>
    <div class="bp-card bp-download-card" data-bp-downloads data-bp-gate="password">
      <h3>Download the app</h3>
      <p class="bp-card-intro">The installers are available to invited producers. Enter the password you received and the download buttons appear; your browser remembers it for a week.</p>
      <div data-bp-downloads-slot><p class="bp-help">Loading...</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="bp-note">The installers are not yet signed with an Apple or Microsoft certificate. On macOS, right-click the app and choose Open the first time; on Windows, choose More info and then Run anyway in the SmartScreen dialog.</p>
    <div class="bp-ai">
      <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><i style="--icon: url('/assets/icons/light-bulb.svg')"></i></span>
      <div>
        <p><strong>The AI runs on your own ChatGPT subscription.</strong> The planner uses the OpenAI Codex command line on the computer where the app runs, signed in with your ChatGPT account. There is no Tubes AI service in between, no API key and no credits: install Codex (<code>npm i -g @openai/codex</code>, then <code>codex login</code>) and the app does the rest.</p>
        <p>Your documents go to the portal only if you upload them there. If we run a production for you, our computer and our ChatGPT subscription do the work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

